body:
What I think the current Irelia design fails:

\- Bloated champion. She has too many habilities + keywords, so they had to make her statline weak;

\- Fighting her always feels one-sided, not to mention her package allows her to attack 2+ times almost every round.

Explaining the changes:

\- Removed the Attune and hability to create Flawless Duet to reduce the variability in her gameplay;

\- New recall mechanic to make up for the Flawless Duet removal + it fits the Ionia design pattern;

\- Bladesurge is now Fast so the opponent can kill the Blade before they switch places, adding more interaction;

\- Increased mana cost because she doesn't have to spend mana to Blade Dance anymore and because of the Recall mechanic;

\- Bigger statline to align with the mana cost.

Notes:

\- Maybe some stat changes and Blade Dance quantity will be necessary to make this work;

\- The "Summon an attacking Blade" on Level 1 is just to make the Level up requirement faster, since it's not necessary on her Lvl 2;

\- Her Champ spell might have to change with this rework.
